# IsoRim VGE prestige vacsuit + helmet (Claude, tools/make_vge_prestige_vacsuit.py, 2026-11-11). stuff_*: multiplied by the
# item's colour (untinted: white undyed), as VGE's mask red; vgepv_* fixed, as VGE's mask black.
# Also uses isorim.mtl stuff_plain (white: pads, pauldrons, helmet shell).
# ---- the template's materials (tools/make_vacsuit.py) this garment uses
newmtl stuff_vac_suit
Kd 0.280 0.280 0.280
newmtl stuff_vac_hole
Kd 0.180 0.180 0.180
newmtl stuff_vac_line
Kd 0.090 0.090 0.090
# ---- VGE prestige: the fixed gold (VGE's mask black)
newmtl vgepv_gold
Kd 0.710 0.600 0.243
# the valves on the gold as a texture: Kd = the gold they sit on, texels = wanted / (Kd x 1.08) (make_vacsuit.texels), so
# with textures off (or an IsoRim before Api 75) the patch is plain gold and the valves go
newmtl vgepv_gold_decal
Kd 0.710 0.600 0.243
map_Kd IsoRim/People/VgePrestigeDecals
# the helmet's breathing filters: the golds dyed with the item (VGE's mask red there)
newmtl stuff_vgepv_gold
Kd 0.710 0.600 0.243
newmtl stuff_vgepv_gold_deep
Kd 0.318 0.263 0.137
